{"data":{"updated_timestamp":"09/11/2026 18:39:28","profile":{"player_id":"107795","last_updated":"09/11/2026 18:39","fullname":"Noor ul Rahman Akakhail","short_display_name":"Noor","name":"Noor ul Rahman","gender":"M","dob":"01/01/2001","date_of_death":null,"place_birth":"Afghanistan","nationality_id":"262","nationality":"Afghanistan","nationality_short_code":"AFG","nick_name":null,"player_skill":{"id":"4","text":"Wicket Keeper","role":"Wicket Keeper"},"batting_style":{"id":"1","text":"Right Handed"},"bowling_style":{"id":"","text":"-"},"writeup":"<p>Born in Kabul in 2001, Noor Rahman is a right-handed wicketkeeper-batter who has risen through Afghanistan's domestic and development pathway. He made his first-class debut for Maiwand Champions in 2023 and quickly showed promise with the bat, accumulating 450 runs in his first seven first-class matches, including two centuries and a highest score of 132. His performances earned him opportunities with Afghanistan A and in the country's List A and T20 competitions.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nRahman's progress gathered further momentum in 2025, when he featured for Hindukush Strikers in first-class cricket before making his mark in the Shpageeza Cricket League with Amo Sharks. His T20 numbers stood out in particular, with a strike rate above 160 across his early domestic career. He also produced a memorable unbeaten 115 for Maiwand Champions, one of the highest scores of his young T20 career, underlining his ability to accelerate in the middle order.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nHis performances at domestic and A-team level eventually earned him a maiden call-up to Afghanistan's T20I squad for the series against Sri Lanka in March 2026. Although he remained uncapped, his selection marked another significant step in his rise, with the selectors identifying him as a top-order wicketkeeper-batter capable of providing another option alongside Rahmanullah Gurbaz.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nRahman continued to strengthen his case through the 2026 domestic season, representing Band-e-Amir Region in List A cricket before turning out for Speen Ghar Tigers in the Shpageeza Cricket League. He scored 91 runs in five innings in the 2026 edition, including a 48 off 17 balls, showcasing the aggressive approach that had become a feature of his T20 game.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nHis progress led to another major milestone when he was named in Afghanistan's squad for the three-match T20I series against India in September 2026. The uncapped wicketkeeper-batter was selected as the second wicketkeeping option behind Gurbaz, with the call-up reflecting the growing faith in his performances across domestic and A-team cricket.&nbsp;</p>","relation":null,"social_details":null,"trophy_cabinet":null,"majorteams":{"team":[{"id":"1188","active":"1","is_primary":"true","is_international":"1","text":"Afghanistan"},{"id":"1550","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Afghanistan A"},{"id":"1602","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Band-e-Amir Region"},{"id":"1608","active":"0","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Amo Sharks"},{"id":"1613","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Speen Ghar Tigers"},{"id":"3091","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Pamir Legends"},{"id":"3092","active":"0","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Hindukush Strikers"},{"id":"3966","active":"0","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Maiwand Champions"},{"id":"5507","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"United Tigers"}]},"international_debut":{"comp_type_id":"3","comp_type":"T20 International - m","match_id":"273950","match_center":"https://www.icc-cricket.com/matches/273950/afghanistan-vs-india","series_id":"15754","series_name":"India in Afghanistan, 3 T20I Series, 2026","match_date":"17/09/2026","for":{"id":"1188","text":"Afghanistan","short_name":"AFG"},"vs":{"id":"4","text":"India","shor